  "id": "Compound::DB01127 - Gene::1586",
  "verbalization": "Econazole, a member of the azole class of antifungal agents, is linked to Cyp17a1 through a series of structural and functional relationships. The evidence suggests that Econazole, through its resemblance to other azole derivatives like Isoconazole and Sertaconazole, shares a common pathway in binding to Cyp17a1. This binding is consistent across multiple paths, with the lowest common ancestors of Econazole and its analogs all pointing to the broader category of Imidazole Antifungal Drugs and Antifungal Agents. The shared mechanism of binding to Cyp17a1 implies that Econazole, as part of this class, may exert its antifungal effects by modulating Cyp17a1 activity, potentially through inhibition or regulation of enzyme function. The integration of these paths highlights a recurring mechanism of interaction between Econazole and Cyp17a1, emphasizing the role of structural similarity and shared biochemical pathways in mediating this relationship.",
